# Sort

Ordering predicates over sequences, written in pure LOGOS and compiled through every execution
tier. `sortSeq` (iter.lg) does the sorting; these answer "is this already in ascending order?"
for integer and real sequences. Auto-imported on reference.

## Note
True if the `Seq of Int` is in non-decreasing (ascending) order — false at the first adjacent pair out of order.

## To isSortedSeq (xs: Seq of Int) -> Bool:
    Let n be length of xs.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is less than n:
        If item i of xs is greater than item (i + 1) of xs:
            Return false.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Return true.

## Note
True if the `Seq of Real` is in non-decreasing (ascending) order — false at the first adjacent pair out of order.

## To isSortedReal (xs: Seq of Real) -> Bool:
    Let n be length of xs.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is less than n:
        If item i of xs is greater than item (i + 1) of xs:
            Return false.
        Set i to i + 1.
    Return true.
